.SS "int Assimp::ExportProperties::GetPropertyInteger (const char * szName, int iErrorReturn = \fR0xffffffff\fP) const"
Get a configuration property\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIszName\fP Name of the property\&. All supported properties are defined in the aiConfig\&.g header (all constants share the prefix AI_CONFIG_XXX)\&. 
.br
\fIiErrorReturn\fP Value that is returned if the property is not found\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Current value of the property 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Property of different types (float, int, string \&.\&.) are kept on different lists, so calling \fBSetPropertyInteger()\fP for a floating-point property has no effect - the loader will call \fBGetPropertyFloat()\fP to read the property, but it won't be there\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const \fBaiMatrix4x4\fP Assimp::ExportProperties::GetPropertyMatrix (const char * szName, const \fBaiMatrix4x4\fP & sErrorReturn = \fR\fBaiMatrix4x4\fP()\fP) const"
Get a matrix configuration property
