.SS "bool Assimp::ExportProperties::SetPropertyInteger (const char * szName, int iValue)"
Set an integer configuration property\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIszName\fP Name of the property\&. All supported properties are defined in the aiConfig\&.g header (all constants share the prefix AI_CONFIG_XXX and are simple strings)\&. 
.br
\fIiValue\fP New value of the property 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if the property was set before\&. The new value replaces the previous value in this case\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Property of different types (float, int, string \&.\&.) are kept on different stacks, so calling \fBSetPropertyInteger()\fP for a floating-point property has no effect - the loader will call \fBGetPropertyFloat()\fP to read the property, but it won't be there\&. 
.RE
.PP

